course: dictionary
lesson: 11500
title: Agitation: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Agitation is a word with three meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Read the clues first. «She paced the room in great agitation, waiting for the phone to ring.» Here agitation means a worried, nervous or upset feeling that makes you restless.
explain: «Stir the mixture slowly, because agitation helps the salt dissolve in the water.» In a science text, agitation means shaking or stirring something, such as a liquid. The clue is the mixture and the salt dissolving.
explain: «Years of agitation by local people led to a new park.» Here agitation means public campaigning or protest, where people work together to make others demand change. The clues are local people and the new park. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word.
fact: Agitation is a noun. You can say «feelings of agitation» or «the agitation of the liquid».
fact: «Agitation» means a worried, nervous or upset feeling that makes you restless.
fact: «Agitation» can also mean shaking or stirring something, such as a liquid.
fact: «Agitation» can mean a campaign: «an agitation» is a public effort to make people demand change.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right: look for feelings in a story, stirring in science, and people campaigning in history.
exercise: «She paced the room in great agitation.» What does agitation show here? | * A worried, nervous, upset feeling | A happy song | A quiet, peaceful nap | A sudden change in the weather
exercise: «Stir the mixture, because agitation helps the salt dissolve.» In this sentence, agitation means | Shaking or stirring the liquid | * Shaking or stirring the liquid | Pouring the liquid away | Freezing the liquid
exercise: «Years of agitation by local people led to a new park.» Find and copy one word that tells you agitation is a campaign. | park | years | local | * people
test: «The fans' agitation grew as the match went to extra time.» What does agitation mean here? | A slow walk | * A restless, nervous, worried feeling | Quiet, calm happiness | Very cold weather
test: «The group started an agitation for a new bus stop.» What does agitation mean here? | A kind of food | A sleepy rest | Mixing paint | * A public campaign to make people demand change
exam: Which sentence uses agitation to mean shaking or stirring? | «He felt agitation before the test.» | «She showed great agitation in her letter.» | * «The agitation of the liquid helped it mix.» | «The campaign for the bus stop began.»
